# HOMA Project — Cursor Rules

## ABSOLUTE RULES — Do Not Violate

1. NEVER auto-commit changes.
2. NEVER auto-push changes to git.
3. NEVER run `git commit` or `git push` without explicit user approval.
4. ALWAYS save changes to the local file first.
5. STOP after editing the file. Do not proceed to git.

## WORKFLOW

When I ask you to make a code change:
- Edit the file in place.
- Save to disk.
- Show me a diff.
- STOP. Wait for my approval.

When I approve, I will:
- Open VS Code
- Verify the change
- Run `npm run build` locally
- Test on localhost:3004
- Run git commands manually in PowerShell

You do NOT do any of these steps. You only edit the file.

## TOOLS

- Cursor (you): edit code only. Stop before git.
- VS Code: view the edited file.
- PowerShell: run `npm run build`, `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`.
- Browser: test locally at localhost:3004.

## WHAT NOT TO DO

- Do not run `git add .`
- Do not run `git commit`
- Do not run `git push`
- Do not run "accept all and commit"
- Do not auto-save multiple files
- Do not edit files outside the one I asked about

## WHAT TO DO

- Make the requested change.
- Save the file locally.
- Show the diff.
- STOP.
- Wait for approval.